# No Cursor git attribution (hard rule)

Cursor must **never** appear as a GitHub contributor on this repo.

## Commits
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made-with: Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any Cursor/agent trailer.
- Do **not** use `git commit --trailer` for Cursor/attribution.
- Commit message = subject + body only, authored as the repo user.
- If a Cursor trailer is injected after commit, strip it before push (amend only when amend rules allow; otherwise new commit without the trailer / rewrite).

## Pull requests
- Do **not** put “Made with Cursor”, “Created by Cursor”, or similar footers in PR titles/bodies.
Prefer `gh pr create --body-file` over inline `--body` when creating PRs.

## Reminder
CLI/project attribution is disabled (`.cursor/cli.json` + `~/.cursor/cli-config.json`). A `commit-msg` hook strips Cursor trailers as a backstop.
